menu "Firefly bring-up (S15 slice b)"

    choice FF_BRINGUP_STAGE
        prompt "Display/touch bring-up stage"
        default FF_BRINGUP_STAGE_1
        help
            S15 slice b is bring-up-in-the-loop: the maintainer flashes one
            stage, looks at the glass, then advances. Each stage is a strict
            superset of the previous one's init, so a dark screen at stage N
            still tells you exactly how far the earlier stages got from the
            serial log. Switch with `idf.py menuconfig` (this menu) or set
            CONFIG_FF_BRINGUP_STAGE=N in sdkconfig before building.

        config FF_BRINGUP_STAGE_1
            bool "Stage 1 - first light (panel only, no LVGL)"
            help
                IO expander up, release LCD_RST + TP_RST, backlight on,
                SPD2010 QSPI panel init, then esp_lcd_panel_draw_bitmap a
                solid fill and a two-colour split. Proves the expander,
                reset release, QSPI wiring, init sequence, RGB565 byte order
                and orientation with no GUI stack in the way.

        config FF_BRINGUP_STAGE_2
            bool "Stage 2 - the app on glass (LVGL v9, one face)"
            help
                Everything in stage 1, then LVGL v9 up via esp_lvgl_port and
                one real ff_shell face rendered (Radar, no selection) — the
                same projection the sim renders for that state.

        config FF_BRINGUP_STAGE_3
            bool "Stage 3 - touch drives it (SPD2010 -> shell input)"
            help
                Everything in stage 2, then the SPD2010 touch controller is
                wired to an LVGL pointer indev so a physical tap/swipe feeds
                the SAME abstract input events the sim ctl socket injects,
                changing shell state.
    endchoice

    config FF_BRINGUP_STAGE
        int
        default 1 if FF_BRINGUP_STAGE_1
        default 2 if FF_BRINGUP_STAGE_2
        default 3 if FF_BRINGUP_STAGE_3

    config FF_DEMO_MODE
        bool "Demo mode — boot into the fictional Firefly Fields world"
        default n
        help
            S20 demo mode (docs/specs/S20-demo-mode.md). When enabled, the
            firmware EMBED_FILES the demo festpack
            (firmware/assets/demo/firefly-fields.festpack.json) and, on
            boot, seeds the shell into "Firefly Fields" via ff_demo_seed:
            a fictional festival lineup, five seeded crew members
            (live / close-range / stale / no-fix) and a Signals feed, with
            the wall clock latched to Saturday 21:30 — so every face shows
            real-looking data with NO mesh, comms brain or real festival.

            The seeded state is genuinely computed through the real core
            APIs (honest freshness/close-range/no-fix), but the mode is a
            DEMO: it does not connect to a radio and shows a fixed,
            frozen world. Leave OFF for field builds. Meaningful at
            bring-up STAGE 2 or 3 (a face must render to see it).

endmenu
